      "explanation": "First find where the original fraction is defined. Since\n\\[\nx^2-5x=x(x-5),\n\\]\nwe must have \\(x\\ne0,5\\). For every allowed value,\n\\[\n\\frac{2x^2-10x}{x^2-5x}\n=\\frac{2x(x-5)}{x(x-5)}=2.\n\\]\nThe equation therefore requires \\(2=x-3\\), giving \\(x=5\\). But this makes the original denominator zero, so it is not a solution. There are \\(\\boxed{0}\\) values of \\(x\\), choice \\(\\mathrm A\\).",
